DTSTART:20261228T063000
DTEND:20261228T070500
SUMMARY:[RW] Swim: technique and aerobic (35 min)
DESCRIPTION:8 min easy swim + kick\; 10 min drills (catch-up\, fingertip d
 rag\, sculling)\; 10 min steady aerobic\, RPE 3\; 5 min cool-down. Swim t
 ime and effort\, not distance: pools and paces differ. If you know your 1
 00 m time\, convert the minutes to metres. Rest 15-30 s between repeats.\
 n\nWeek 6 (BUILD). Not medical advice\; pain that changes how you move me
 ans stop.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-12-28-str1-strength-lower-body-@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003913Z
DTSTART:20261228T183000
DTEND:20261228T185500
SUMMARY:[RW] Strength: lower body (glutes and single-leg stability) (25 mi
 n)
DESCRIPTION:Endurance (running\, cycling): better economy and injury resis
 tance without costing the key aerobic sessions. Lift with 2-3 reps in res
 erve\, stop a set if form breaks. Strength starts at least 3 hours after 
 cardio (practice).\n\nWeek 6 (BUILD). Not medical advice\; pain that chan
 ges how you move means stop.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-12-29-swim4-swim-aerobic-enduran@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003913Z
DTSTART:20261229T063000
DTEND:20261229T070500
SUMMARY:[RW] Swim: aerobic endurance (35 min)
DESCRIPTION:8 min easy swim\; 15 min steady aerobic with a few 25 m kicks\
 ; 5 min cool-down. Swim time and effort\, not distance: pools and paces d
 iffer. If you know your 100 m time\, convert the minutes to metres. Rest 
 15-30 s between repeats.\n\nWeek 6 (BUILD). Not medical advice\; pain tha
 t changes how you move means stop.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
